foreign  Costa and I run Pinnacle Stone  Restoration we are specialized in  restoration of Terrazzo and natural  stone surfaces  I'm going to walk you through how to  restore over 100 years old Terrazzo that  is covered in carpet  [Music]  the most difficult part of this  restoration is carpet and glue removal  we remove carpet with electric scraping  machines  it also can be done by hand but electric  scraping machines do much faster and a  better job  the project is taking place in historic  University dormitory the client decided  to restore existing Terrazzo rather than  replacing carpet costs carpet  accumulates a lot of dust and bacteria  generally Terrazzo is indestructible  surface also it's an easy maintenance  we are discovering multiple issues with  this Terrazzo carpet glue missing  Terrazzo surface cracks and gouge nail  holes it's repairable and requires a lot  of work  the next step we are removing carpet  glue we are removing carpet glue with a  handheld scrapers  versus using grinding process when we  use a grinding process we can activate  the quality of the glue and it will  become sticky but by hand we keep the  temperature low and the glue it just  comes out very easy from terrazzo  then we grind terrazzo floors with  grinding machines we use Diamond discs  we use a coarse medium fine grits to  flatten terrazzoid it's very important  to level and flatten terrazzo floor for  honing process even for polishing  process and this particular project we  are going to use a dry grinding process  just because we want to see the process  during the wet grinding process and the  slurry that is produced during the  grinding prevents us to see the details  of the terrazzo  [Music]  after grinding process is completed we  left with multiple nail holes and cracks  to prepare them for a patchwork we  approach each like a dentist and we  clean them out like in cavity  then Aggregates go into the laws  and when it cures it will be ready to be  grind down to flatten and to level it to  the existing terrazole  the next step of restoration process is  honing which is done with diamond pads  we use water of course to lubricate the  diamonds so lowest grid will be 50 grit  followed by 120 220 400 and 800 Degrees  what only process does it ensures that  no scratches Left Behind the grinding  process  since it's a wet process it will  accumulate a lot of slurry that has to  be extracted by wet vacuums followed by  Edge work  so Edge work is area that bigger  machines don't reach those tight areas  so every step does to happen with  handheld machines in a smaller scales  grinding process to honing process to  reach those tight areas to develop the  same Sheen as rest of the surface  the next step is the polishing is 800  grit completes the honing process 1500  grit starts polishing process so 1500  grit followed by 3000 Grit  and after that we use VIP systems this  is much finer Diamond pads  when you polish Terrazzo you increasing  the density of Terrazzo so it becomes  more durable because you're closing  those poles that's automatically makes  Terrazzo harder and more durable  and now it's time to seal reusing micro  tapping sealer it's more like  impregnating sealer that goes into  Terrazzo and it prevents Terrazzo from  staining and it protects it the last  step is burnishing burnishing helps  sealer to bring the terrazzo to its  highest Gene  if I have to compare this project to  other projects that we've done I would  say this stands for number 10 for sure  because there are a lot of obstacles  that we have to go through and uh  Terrazzo is original and I have to  mention that it's about 5 000 square  feet

